# Every arrowhead at once, and a flaming one on top of them. The buff is the
# quiet half -- 15% final damage and 20% attack for 40 seconds -- and the
# flaming arrows are the whole of the damage.
#
# One trigger fires six arrows, each its own attack of nine lines on six
# enemies, and the six are consecutive rather than spread: GMS's "Duration: 5
# sec." is how long an arrow hunts for a target, which is why namuwiki prizes
# the long flight for farming. Namu prints the total outright, 534,600%, and
# that is 6 arrows x 18 volleys x 9 lines x 550% exactly.
#
# The stock is eighteen volleys on a 2-second re-trigger, so it runs dry at 36
# seconds of the 40-second buff -- the tooltip's own warning that the attack
# stops while the buff still stands. GMS fires it "upon attack"; this game's
# swing clock never idles, so that is simply the 2 seconds.
#
# The attack percentage joins the same pool Marksmanship's does. GMS writes
# this one indiePadR against Marksmanship's plain padR, but one pool is what
# this game has, and namuwiki's own spec table sums the pair to 45% too.
name: "Quiver Barrage"
description:
  "Fire every type of arrowhead at once, including a special flaming arrowhead "
  "that explodes when it hits an enemy. The Flaming Arrow targets the boss "
  "with the highest HP first and is unaffected by attack reflection. The "
  "Flaming Arrow is prepared in limited quantities and will no longer attack "
  "once used up."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 3 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
buff {
  duration_seconds: 40.0
  base { final_dmg_pct: 0.15 attack_pct: 0.055 }
  per_level { attack_pct: 0.005 }
  pulse {
    label: "Flaming Arrow"
    cast_interval_seconds: 2.0
    casts: 6
    max_enemies: 6
    lines: 9
    max_pulses: 18
    base { skill_pct: 2.60 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.10 }
  }
}
